load @term/seed/code/structure/ring
  find ring

# A unit: an invertible element of a ring, one with a multiplicative inverse also in the ring. The units of a ring form
# a group under multiplication. In a field every nonzero element is a unit, and in the integers only one and minus one
# are. The unit quaternions, the units of the Hurwitz quaternion ring, are the twenty-four points of the 24-cell. The
# form carries the ring; being a unit is the property of having an inverse.
form unit
  link ring, like ring
